From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:20:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: Dolby Vision Standard tunnel on DCN 4.2 and
 4.2B, with a read back of the pipe

linux-9910 offers DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB on the display pipelines it was
reviewed for, and linux-9947 added DCN 4.0.1. DCN 4.2 (GC 11.5.4) and
DCN 4.2B (a variant of GC 11.5.0), the display cores of the newest AMD
APUs, were left out: they have resources, a DPP, an MPC and a sequencer
of their own (dcn42, dcn42b). On them Dolby Vision played as HDR10.

Reviewed stage by stage in 7.3.4, with the state that linux-9910,
linux-9947 and linux-9973 require (XRGB8888 primary plane alone,
unscaled, opaque; no plane or CRTC colour properties; COLOR_SPACE_SRGB;
RGB 8 bpc over TMDS; DITHER_OPTION_TRUN8):

- every stage is programmed with the functions of DCN 4.0.1: the format
  converter, post-CSC, pre-degamma, gamma correction, HDR multiplier,
  dealpha and bias of the DPP (dpp3_*(), dpp35_program_bias_and_scale_fcnv()),
  the scaler through SPL (dpp401_dscl_set_scaler_manual_scale(), the same
  SPL callbacks), the output gamma, output CSC, gamut remaps and MCM of
  the MPC (mpc3_*(), mpc32_*(), mpc401_*()), the formatter of the OPP of
  DCN 2 (opp1_*()) and the dcn401 sequencer;
- of their own: dpp42_dpp_setup(), that of DCN 4.0.1 but for the alpha
  LUT of 2-bit alpha formats; dcn42_update_mpcc() and
  mpc42_update_blending(), whose global alpha and gain are 12 bits wide,
  in MPCC_CONTROL2, opaque at 0xfff; dcn42_set_mcm_luts(), the MCM of DCN
  4.0.1 and the RMCM, only for a plane with rmcm_enable, which the tunnel
  refuses with every other cm flag; dcn42_program_cm_hist(), a colour
  histogram that a surface update can turn on, now refused with the
  tunnel; and an HDMI encoder that puts the AVI InfoFrame and the vendor
  one in generic packets 0 and 1, as enc3 does on DCN 4.0.1;
- every register and field that those functions write for the tunnel
  is in the register lists of both pools with a mask that is not zero,
  as in the list of DCN 4.0.1. Read from the preprocessed resource files
  of the three pools: the fields without a mask are in functions that
  these pools do not use, in the clocks of the DPP and in the debug
  option cm_in_bypass; the casts of the DPP and MPC structures between
  generations find the same members in front;
- three blocks are never programmed by DC on DCN and keep what the VBIOS
  or a reset left there: the pre-CSC of the format converter, the
  denormalisation of the MPC output and, in this kernel, the RMCM
  (nothing allocates it; Linux 7.4 notes that MPC_RMCM_CNTL may still
  hold a boot value, 8728be7e2305).

Fail-closed, and saying what it found:

- once DC has validated the context, amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_check_dcn42()
  checks what it will program for the pipes of each tunnelled stream:
  one plane, on one pipe per ODM slice and none blended over another, at
  most four, no sub-viewport; the scaler that SPL computed for each pipe
  in 444 bypass or DSCL bypass, with one tap and EASF and ISHARP off; the
  bit depth reduction of DITHER_OPTION_TRUN8 and no clamp in the
  formatter. Anything else refuses the commit, as "scanout" in
  DVBRIDGE_REFUSED and in the kernel log with the reason; user space
  keeps the display as it was and plays HDR10;
- each time the tunnel goes on, dc_stream_read_byte_tunnel_dcn42() reads
  back from their registers the DPP and the MPCC of each pipe, the MPC
  output and the formatter of each OPP, the two RMCM and the HDMI
  encoder, the three blocks above among them, into the kernel log, with
  what is not as the tunnel needs. A field for which the pool has no
  register or no mask (a read of either gives 0, which would look like a
  bypass) counts as not read. A read back that is not as the tunnel
  needs refuses the tunnel from the next commit that turns it on, until
  the driver is loaded again: user space plays HDR10 from then on;
- the output transfer function must be bypass at commit setup, as on
  DCN 4.0.1.

DCN 2.0.1 and 6.0 stay out, and the kernel log now says so once.

Host test: the judge of the read back, the check of the validated pipes,
the check of the plane and the gate, cut out of this file onto mock
types: 241 checks. The state that DC programs for the tunnel, on one pipe
and on two ODM slices, and nine variants of it that keep the bytes pass;
79 changes of the read back, 20 of the validated pipes and 3 of the plane
are each refused for their own reason; the gate offers the tunnel on DCN
4.2 and 4.2B, still on DCN 1 to 3.6 and 4.0.1, and not on DCN 2.0.1 or
6.0. 42 mutations of the code, each caught. An audit of the 90
fields that the read back takes finds a register and a mask for each in
both pools. W=1 of the 612 objects of the AMD display code: no new
warning.

Not tried on hardware: no DCN 4.2 or 4.2B machine is at hand. What
cannot be read from the code: the semantics of the registers, among them
whether the blocks that DC never programs pass the bytes in the state
the read back finds. The read back in the kernel log is there for the
first test.
